        "content": "Read one document and report what it says in answer to a question. Use only this document: nothing you know from elsewhere, and no guesses.\n\nQuestion: Which sports team does Giovanni Delfino represent or represent?\n\nDocument:\nGiovanni Delfino\n\nGiovanni Delfino is an Italian association football player who currently plays for Uberlândia E.C., a Brazilian football team. Early Life and Career\n\nGiovanni Delfino was born on February 12, 1995, in Milan, Italy. He began his football career at a young age, playing for local clubs in the Milan region. In 2012, he joined the youth academy of A.C. Milan, one of Italy's most prestigious football clubs. Professional Career\n\nDelfino made his professional debut for A.C. Milan in 2015, coming on as a substitute in a Serie A match against Inter Milan. He went on to make several appearances for the club before being loaned out to Serie B side, Virtus Entella, in 2017. In 2019, Delfino made the move to Brazil, signing with Uberlândia E.C. in the Campeonato Brasileiro Série B. Since joining the club, he has become a regular starter and has scored several important goals. Studies and References\n\nA study published in the Journal of Sports Science and Medicine in 2020 found that Delfino's move to Uberlândia E.C. had a significant impact on his performance, with his goal-scoring rate increasing by 25% compared to his time in Italy. [1]\n\nIn an interview with Brazilian sports magazine, Placar, in 2020, Delfino stated, \"I'm very happy to be playing for Uberlândia E.C. The team has been very welcoming, and I'm enjoying the challenge of playing in a new country.\" [2]\n\nA report by Brazilian football website, Globo Esporte, in 2020, listed Delfino as one of the top foreign players in the Campeonato Brasileiro Série B, citing his impressive goal-scoring record and consistent performances. [3]\n\nReferences\n\n[1] Journal of Sports Science and Medicine, Volume 23, Issue 2, 2020, pp. 123-128. [2] Placar, Issue 